{
  "description": "Fork release versions X.Y.Z-ch.N. Read by the firmware's host tests (test/game_core) and meant for the fork release workflow's checks. A tag matches tag_grammar as a whole string (a POSIX ERE that also works in Python and ECMAScript; capture group 4 is N; in Python use re.fullmatch, since $ alone accepts a trailing newline) and is at most max_tag_length characters. A running version has N only when a prefix is a tag followed by the end, - or +; otherwise N is 0. Only N decides newer. An empty asset means no asset name exists for that input.",
  "tag_grammar": "^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)[.](0|[1-9][0-9]*)[.](0|[1-9][0-9]*)-ch[.]([1-9][0-9]{0,8})$",
